  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The RNA-only baseline (config_018, scgpt, avgpool) achieves 0.530 accuracy, outperforming both multimodal configs with resnet50 (config_001: 0.512 concat, config_004: 0.525 weighted). This suggests resnet50 image features are not adding value, but we have not yet tested whether a stronger image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) changes this picture. Question: Does replacing resnet50 with imagenet_vit_l (while holding all other settings constant: scgpt, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted fusion) make the image modality informative enough to close or reverse the gap to the RNA-only baseline? Why this is the best next experiment: It is a clean single-variable comparison against config_004 (only image encoder changes), directly isolating the effect of image representation quality. The result will clarify whether the image modality has any utility at all, which is the most consequential architectural decision remaining. If config_031 still underperforms config_018, it strongly suggests image features are not contributing and we should focus on RNA encoder/aggregation choices. If it matches or exceeds config_018, it validates the multimodal direction and motivates further fusion/aggregation exploration."
}

